@meta
id: 22-11
title: The slow way, measured
chapter: 22
type: lesson
skills: visual-char, visual-line
par: 50
minutes: 6
vscode: this is the VS Code way, and it is why you are here
open: order.provider.ts

@brief
Two jobs in one file. `legacyRefund` is dead and goes, the whole
method and the blank line after it. And `total` is renamed `amount` in
the three places it appears.

Do it with visual mode first if you like: `V`, count down the method
with `j`, `d`; `viw`, `c`, type the word. It will pass the file check.
It will not pass par. Par is set to the operator route from chapters
8 to 11, plus a little, and the visual route does not fit under it.

Then `./dojo replay` and do it the other way.

@keys
| `dap` | delete a paragraph — the method and the blank line after it |
| `ciw` | change the word under the cursor |
| `n` `.` | next match, repeat the change |

@hints
A method with no blank lines inside it is a paragraph. From any line
of it, one operator and one text object take the whole thing.
--
`ciw` on the first `total`, type `amount`, `Esc`. `n` finds the next
`total`, `.` repeats the change. There are three.
--
`/legacyRefund` `Enter`, `dap`. `/\<total\>` `Enter`, `ciwamount`
`Esc`, `n.`, `n.`.

@solution
    /legacyRefund<Enter> d a p /\<total\><Enter> c i w amount <Esc> n . n . :wq<Enter>

Forty-six keystrokes. The visual version of the same edit —
`V` and ten `j` and `d` for the method, `viwcamount` then `n.` twice —
comes to fifty-six, and that is on a ten-line method. On a forty-line
method the counted `j` would be the whole budget.

The two habits to keep from this: name the region with a text object
when it has a name (`ap`, `iw`, `i{`), and let `.` do the repetition.
Visual mode wins when the region has no name — an odd span of a
sentence, half a call, a column. Everything from lesson 12 onward is
one of those.

@start order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
  ) {}

  public async legacyRefund(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });
    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }
    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }
    return this.paymentService.refundLegacy(order.id, order.total);
  }

  public async refund(id: string, total: number) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    if (total > order.paid) {
      throw exception('REFUND_EXCEEDS_ORDER');
    }

    return this.paymentService.refund(order.id, total);
  }
}

@expected order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
  ) {}

  public async refund(id: string, amount: number) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    if (amount > order.paid) {
      throw exception('REFUND_EXCEEDS_ORDER');
    }

    return this.paymentService.refund(order.id, amount);
  }
}
